
==========================================================================
WARNING: security.grpc.enforcement = "legacy" disables per-method tier authorization.

Every authenticated client of a read_write listener may call every
method up to that listener's max_tier cap, including the
operator_only methods that reconfigure the daemon; the
[security.grpc.roles] entries are recorded as audit context and deny
nothing. Tier enforcement is the default since v0.24.0 and becomes
mandatory in a future release, which will reject this config.

To migrate: give every listener a role identity — mTLS listeners
derive it from the client certificate, bearer-token TCP and UDS
listeners need an explicit `principal` — map each principal in
[security.grpc.roles] to observer, automation, or operator, then set
security.grpc.enforcement = "tier". See
docs/adr/0064-grpc-authorization.md and docs/SECURITY.md.
==========================================================================

